# Blank layers: geom_blank

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`geom_blank()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/geom_blank.html), in the order the page
gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly cannot
draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a list of
what remains.

`geom_blank()` draws nothing, but its data still sets the plot's scales, which makes it a way of
giving several plots the same scales; the page points to `expand_limits()` for more. Giggly has no
`geom_blank()` yet.

## A plot with no layers

```r
ggplot(mtcars, aes(wt, mpg))
# Nothing to see here!
```

ggplot2 draws a plot with no layers as though it had a `geom_blank()` layer: no marks, but axes
that span `wt` and `mpg` and are titled by them. Not in Giggly yet: `geom_blank()`.
